# Userspace watchdog heartbeat

The Linux image owns the PMIC PON watchdog from userspace (`/init` forks a
daemon that opens `/dev/watchdog` and only pings while the host writes to the
second ACM port, `/dev/ttyACM1`).

Observed on the phone (pstore console, no host heartbeat):

```text
[    1.566100] gkiw-wdt: 30s timeout, heartbeat on /dev/ttyGS1
[    2.567422] gkiw-wdt: host heartbeat started
[   25.824993] gkiw-wdt: host heartbeat lost
[   54.827664] watchdog0: pretimeout event
```

The first heartbeat is ModemManager probing the new port; it stops after about
20 s and the phone resets 30 s after the last ping.

Positive test with `global/harness/2ndstage/host/gkiw-heartbeat /dev/ttyACM1`:
the phone stayed up past 91 s of uptime. Stopping the host helper then reset
the phone 36 s later (30 s timeout plus the 5 s heartbeat window).
